  "description": "Event Details Date: 22 October 2026 Time: 11:00 AM – 1:30 PM Venue: Naidu Hall, I.T.S Engineering College, Greater Noida Registration Fee: ₹300 per team Prize Pool: ₹15,000 (₹7,000 / ₹5,000 / ₹3,000) + Free Incubation Team Size: 2 participants per team Coordinator: Miss. Anushka Tyagi Event Description Junior Ideathon is an opportunity for school students to identify pressing problems around them and develop innovative solutions with clear implementation planning. Participants present their ideas using a PPT/PDF pitch deck and explain the problem, proposed solution, feasibility, impact, and scalability before the jury. Guidelines Participants must report to the venue on time Carry a valid School ID Card for verification The presentation must be submitted in PPT/PDF format 10–15 minutes before the event begins Each team gets 5 minutes for the presentation, followed by 2 minutes of Q&A Judging Criteria Criteria Weightage Problem Identification 15% Innovation 25% Feasibility 20% Impact 20% Presentation 10% Scalability 10% Disqualification The following will result in disqualification: Misconduct Cheating or plagiarism External assistance Misrepresentation of participant identity Any violation of the general event rules The final decision rests with the jury and organizing committee. Opportunities for Winners: Incubation Support — Up to ₹90,000 Get incubation support worth up to ₹90,000 for 18 months to develop and scale your innovative idea. Get Truscholar credits -- Up to ₹14.2+ Lakhs Expert Mentorship Receive guidance from industry experts and experienced mentors to refine your idea, strategy, and business model. Product Development Support Get hands-on support to build, test, and refine your product and turn your idea into a market-ready solution.",
